  "releaseNote": "Harden signed session acceptance, owned request lifetimes and receipt disclosure; preserve action uncertainty and current evidence; validate device responses and complete numeric XDR evidence; preserve disjoint candidate validity intervals and scoped evidence; recover UI state and focus; validate measurement rounding and bounded policies; isolate Git fixture contexts; attribute launcher readiness to the owned child; preserve startup guidance and verify exact source commits across CI platforms; synchronize browser recovery checks with completed UI state and atomic manual actions. Preserve original course and historical evidence. Require independently recognized normal activity and valid observation provenance before applying XDR source or destination exemptions; preserve unknown and malformed observations without erasing valid candidates. Retain partial native operation ownership through clock, binding and final continuation failures. Carry operation and proof deadlines through queued native exchanges; preserve callback ownership in both connection controllers and reject cancellation during final measurement timestamps. Share owned absolute-deadline timers across sensors, connection waiters and retained flows, browser native requests and server support; preserve exact parent ceilings, the full browser local cap, cancellation causes and bounded cleanup."
